course: dictionary
lesson: 7506
title: Potions and make-believe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A potion is a drink made from mixed liquids that is supposed to have a special effect, such as magic, medicine or poison. Read the words around the word to find its meaning: «In cartoons a character drinks a potion and shoots up overnight.» Shooting up overnight is not something real bodies do, so the potion here is make-believe.
explain: The next part of the sentence gives a clue too: real growing is slow, steady and full of surprises. The writer is contrasting pretend growth with real growth, so you know the potion belongs to pretend stories and cartoons.
explain: In stories witches and wizards brew potions in cauldrons, and in games a health potion restores lives. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a magic drink that heals" fits, so your meaning is right.
explain: Never drink or mix an unknown liquid, even in a game or a story. A potion in a book is pretend, but a real bottle of liquid could be harmful.
fact: A potion is a drink made from mixed liquids, supposed to have a special effect.
fact: In fairy tales and fantasy games, a potion can heal, make someone sleep, fall in love or change shape.
fact: To brew a potion means to mix ingredients together to make it.
fact: Long ago, potions were old medicines, and many were useless or dangerous.
fact: Never drink or mix an unknown liquid, even in a game.
exercise: «In cartoons a character drinks a potion and shoots up overnight.» What is a potion? | A sweet made from fruit | *A drink made from mixed liquids, with a special effect | A type of shoe worn by wizards | A cloud that makes you tall
exercise: In a fantasy game, what does a health potion do? | Turns your hair white | *Restores your lives | Makes you fall asleep for a hundred years | Changes the colour of the screen
exercise: Which is the safe rule? | Mix liquids together to see what happens | *Never drink an unknown liquid, even in a game | Share a bottle of unknown liquid with friends | Drink any liquid you find in a game
test: In the phrase «sleeping potion», what effect does the potion have? | Makes you wide awake | Makes you grow taller | Makes you laugh | *Makes you sleep
test: In «In cartoons a character drinks a potion and shoots up overnight», what tells you the growth is not real? | The word character | The word potion | The word cartoons | *The contrast with real growing, which is slow and steady
exam: Which best describes a potion in a fantasy game? | *A magic drink that heals, makes you sleep or changes your shape | A pet dog | A sports score | A type of dance
